      "body": "- `test_sparse_mla_backends.py`: `test_hisparse_staged_prefill_cache_backs_min_attention_rows` builds a bare `HiSparseRuntime` with `cache_ops` from the platform backend instead of passing `self=None`\n\n#61659 added this test calling `HiSparseRuntime.gather_prefill_cache(None, host_cache, plan)`, written against the version where the method called `torch.ops._C_cache_ops` directly. #62592 had already moved that call behind `self.cache_ops` from the HiSparse platform backend, so on main the test fails with `AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'cache_ops'` in (B200) V1 Attention Shard 4/6 and (H100) V1 Attention Shard 1/5 (e.g. https://buildkite.com/vllm/ci/builds/97806), and on every PR that runs those shards. The test now sets up the runtime the same way `HiSparseRuntime` does for itself; the assertions are unchanged. I checked the old and new calls against main's runtime code with the CUDA op stubbed: the old call raises the same error, the new one passes the test's assertions.\n\nAI assistance (Claude Code) was used to draft this change. Every line was reviewed by the submitter.\n",
